      "chunks": [
        {
          "id": 114,
          "content": "# Scheduler architecture\nMeridian separates ownership, planning, execution and display to permit independent restarts.\n## Planner\nThe planner solves interval conflicts using instrument availability and reservation priority. It can compute a plan while execution is suspended. A computed plan is not permission to bypass a weather interlock or clock check.\n## Prototype recovery\nThe retired prototype cleared pending reservations when time drifted and restarted on its first local clock sample. These behaviours must not be used to recover the current gateway.",
          "metadata": "{\"types\":[\"heading\",\"text\"],\"level\":1,\"path\":[\"Scheduler architecture\",\"Prototype recovery\"]}",
          "sort_order": 0,
          "embedding_bytes": null,
          "sha256": "f8627ae4ac8eb1d3ddb3a6ac1d67d63401c58287bef56826c05bc728c7551a8b",
          "exact_source_substring": false,
          "source_line_span": null
        }
      ],
