      "depth": 0,
      "source_content_type": "text/markdown",
      "content_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vanilla1999/DocAtlas/e62fa9e357bd22731cddabe930532a4a2faecc18/eval/blind_project_context/step14-host-language-live/frozen-corpus/weather.md",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "id": 121,
          "content": "# Weather decisions\nWeather decisions govern execution, not ownership of reservations.\n## Suspension\nSuspend outdoor observations when the wind interlock opens. Preserve reservation identifiers during suspension. Resume only after the interlock closes and the duty operator records a restart approval.\n## Indoor instrument\nAn instrument explicitly classified as indoor may continue during a wind suspension, provided its own safety interlocks remain closed. A roof visible as closed on the calendar does not establish indoor classification.",
          "metadata": "{\"types\":[\"heading\",\"text\"],\"level\":1,\"path\":[\"Weather decisions\",\"Indoor instrument\"]}",
          "sort_order": 0,
          "embedding_bytes": null,
          "sha256": "652f8aaa77df45a4cafd17a4c4f779986bee7c5b513ce6e12a5107ecab7584a9",
          "exact_source_substring": false,
          "source_line_span": null
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "content": "## Forecast display\nThe forecast panel predicts wind for planning. A favourable forecast is not an interlock signal and cannot authorize a restart.",
          "metadata": "{\"types\":[\"heading\",\"text\"],\"level\":2,\"path\":[\"Weather decisions\",\"Forecast display\"]}",
          "sort_order": 1,
          "embedding_bytes": null,
          "sha256": "6dcd93ce777f43c3e467ac3519b6a08f1a1368dfead3a55f80a929f0387b9dba",
          "exact_source_substring": false,
          "source_line_span": null
        }
      ],
